WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:01.628
- Good morning Believe nation,

00:00:01.628 --> 00:00:04.803
today's message is, give it your all.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.286
Over to you Jeremy Lin.

00:00:06.286 --> 00:00:08.771
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.771 --> 00:00:11.253
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.253 --> 00:00:14.059
♫ Enspresso keep me going

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:18.234
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.478
- [Jeremy] It's easy to dream big.

00:00:20.478 --> 00:00:23.465
There's the initial
excitement, raw passion,

00:00:23.465 --> 00:00:27.414
high hopes, and you put
in everything you have

00:00:27.414 --> 00:00:29.164
to pursue your dream.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.423
But inevitably the hits will come.

00:00:34.817 --> 00:00:37.400
(upbeat music)

00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:42.531
You get knocked down, you get back up.

00:00:42.531 --> 00:00:44.778
You get knocked down
again, and get back up.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.772
But the criticism keeps coming.

00:00:46.772 --> 00:00:48.951
The hard work doesn't
seem to be paying off.

00:00:48.951 --> 00:00:51.480
One unmet expectation after another

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.064
leads to disappointment, discouragement,

00:00:54.064 --> 00:00:55.897
and even worse, doubt.

00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:01.376
Maybe they're right.

00:01:02.325 --> 00:01:06.075
Maybe I'll never be who
I thought I would be.

00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:08.812
So what will I do?

00:01:09.671 --> 00:01:12.628
I'll work harder than I ever have before.

00:01:12.628 --> 00:01:15.665
I'll work on my weaknesses,
and refine my strengths.

00:01:15.665 --> 00:01:19.638
Give more even after I
thought I gave it my all.

00:01:19.638 --> 00:01:21.532
- Chances are you're
going to quit too soon.

00:01:21.532 --> 00:01:23.768
Chances are you're going to
stop just as you're about

00:01:23.768 --> 00:01:25.518
to make your big breakthrough.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.235
Chances are you're going
to regret not saying yes

00:01:28.235 --> 00:01:30.426
and not continuing on.

00:01:30.426 --> 00:01:32.013
I've told this story a number of times,

00:01:32.013 --> 00:01:34.088
but the toughest decision I
ever had to make in my life

00:01:34.088 --> 00:01:34.921
was when I was in University.

00:01:34.921 --> 00:01:37.479
I had to decide between
the high paying job

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.296
I thought I always wanted,

00:01:39.296 --> 00:01:41.322
and my business that was sucking,

00:01:41.322 --> 00:01:43.512
that I was making $300 a month at,

00:01:43.512 --> 00:01:46.085
and I couldn't get the momentum
that I was looking for.

00:01:46.085 --> 00:01:48.111
And the easy, safe, practical thing to do

00:01:48.111 --> 00:01:50.268
would have been to take the job,

00:01:50.268 --> 00:01:53.869
but I felt like I didn't
give my all to my business.

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:56.578
And I needed to give it
a little bit more time.

00:01:56.578 --> 00:01:58.434
Just so that I would know.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:02.396
Just so that I would know if
this thing would work or not.

00:02:02.396 --> 00:02:04.422
And so I decided to take a year off,

00:02:04.422 --> 00:02:06.490
while some of my friends
are off doing, you know

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.224
traveling the world and
going off and exploring.

00:02:09.224 --> 00:02:12.641
I said, you know what, I'm
going to take one year,

00:02:12.641 --> 00:02:14.837
and I'm going to give everything
I have to this business.

00:02:14.837 --> 00:02:16.187
And I'm going to see
if I can make it work.

00:02:16.187 --> 00:02:18.062
And it may not work,

00:02:18.062 --> 00:02:19.959
the odds are that it's not going to work.

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:22.826
Most businesses don't work,
and up until that point,

00:02:22.826 --> 00:02:24.828
everything that I've done
had shown that my business

00:02:24.828 --> 00:02:26.930
was not working, but I still felt like

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.388
I had more gas in the tank.

00:02:28.388 --> 00:02:31.070
I still felt like even
though I gave it a lot,

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:34.599
I had not given my all,
and I needed to know.

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:38.007
I needed to know, I could
deal with it not working out,

00:02:38.007 --> 00:02:40.397
and me walking away
knowing that that's it,

00:02:40.397 --> 00:02:41.985
I gave it everything I
had, there was nothing else

00:02:41.985 --> 00:02:43.823
that I left on the table.

00:02:43.823 --> 00:02:46.016
That was the best that I could have done.

00:02:46.016 --> 00:02:48.467
If I did that, and it
didn't work, I'm good.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:52.257
But if I didn't do it, if
you don't give it your all,

00:02:52.257 --> 00:02:54.799
if you don't push yourself
to the absolute max,

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:58.389
and it doesn't work out, you will forever

00:02:58.389 --> 00:03:00.056
look back and think,

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.123
maybe it could have worked.

00:03:06.123 --> 00:03:08.805
That's the rest of your life
that you're dealing with.

00:03:08.805 --> 00:03:12.263
And I don't want that to be your story.

00:03:12.263 --> 00:03:14.537
I don't want you to look back on your life

00:03:14.537 --> 00:03:16.841
and regret not having done more,

00:03:16.841 --> 00:03:17.923
not having pushed harder.

00:03:17.923 --> 00:03:21.679
Because that pain is for
the rest of your life.

00:03:21.679 --> 00:03:24.452
That pain is immense, it's huge.

00:03:24.452 --> 00:03:26.837
Versus the short term pain
of whatever you have to do

00:03:26.837 --> 00:03:29.340
right now to give it your all,

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.243
to push a little harder, right.

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:34.008
To push through those extra
hours, to push through those

00:03:34.008 --> 00:03:36.370
extra sets, to push
through that extra work.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.811
It's painful, it sucks,
but it's nothing compared

00:03:39.811 --> 00:03:43.507
to the lifetime of pain and
regret that is ahead of you

00:03:43.507 --> 00:03:45.762
if you don't give it your all.

00:03:45.762 --> 00:03:48.831
So if you're on the verge
of quitting something,

00:03:48.831 --> 00:03:53.141
a relationship, a business,
a partnership, a customer.

00:03:53.141 --> 00:03:57.103
If you're on the verge
of quitting something,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:00.963
maybe the answer is to quit,
but I would ask yourself,

00:04:00.963 --> 00:04:04.008
am I going to regret
walking away from this?

00:04:04.008 --> 00:04:07.509
Did I give this situation everything I had

00:04:07.509 --> 00:04:09.611
so that I'm confident that walking away

00:04:09.611 --> 00:04:11.472
is the right thing to do.

00:04:11.472 --> 00:04:13.804
It's not just the easy thing to do,

00:04:13.804 --> 00:04:17.707
it's the right thing to do
because you gave it your all.

00:04:17.707 --> 00:04:21.097
Don't quit too soon,
don't quit just before

00:04:21.097 --> 00:04:23.555
you make your big breakthrough.

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:26.234
Quit after you've given it your all.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.624
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:04:28.624 --> 00:04:32.922
what percentage, out of
100 words, given everything

00:04:32.922 --> 00:04:37.089
you've got, 100%, out of
that, where do you fall?

00:04:38.099 --> 00:04:40.394
What are you giving to
your business right now?

00:04:40.394 --> 00:04:43.166
Be honest, it's great to say 110%,

00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:44.710
you can't go over 100%.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.755
100% is the max, you're
not playing at your max.

00:04:47.755 --> 00:04:51.419
Be honest, where are you
right now, percentage wise?

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:53.234
I'm curious to find out, leave it down

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:54.592
in the comments below.

00:04:54.592 --> 00:04:56.145
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:04:56.145 --> 00:04:58.207
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Nasr Leon,

00:04:58.207 --> 00:05:00.189
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:00.189 --> 00:05:01.719
Your One Word, I really, really,

00:05:01.719 --> 00:05:04.193
really appreciate your support.

00:05:04.193 --> 00:05:05.605
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.602
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:05:07.602 --> 00:05:10.560
in yourself and whatever your one word is,

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.967
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:11.967 --> 00:05:14.844
for another shot of Enspresso.

00:05:14.844 --> 00:05:17.618
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:17.618 --> 00:05:20.918
♫ Enspresso keep me going

00:05:20.918 --> 00:05:23.160
- Hey Believe nation, thank
you so much for watching.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.220
If you want to learn
more about this subject,

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.736
get a little bit deeper on it,

00:05:26.736 --> 00:05:28.430
I'm going to share some extra bonus clips

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.402
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:05:30.402 --> 00:05:33.493
- How do you want to be
remembered as a football player,

00:05:33.493 --> 00:05:35.175
as a person these last
22 years and everything

00:05:35.175 --> 00:05:36.562
that you've achieved.

00:05:36.562 --> 00:05:38.794
As someone who did achieve a lot,

00:05:38.794 --> 00:05:41.250
what's most important to you?

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.413
- I just want people to see me
as a hard working footballer,

00:05:45.413 --> 00:05:46.975
someone that's passionate about the game,

00:05:46.975 --> 00:05:49.746
and someone that every time
I stepped on the pitch,

00:05:49.746 --> 00:05:53.658
I've given everything
that I have because that's

00:05:53.658 --> 00:05:56.075
how I feel going in to games.

00:05:57.187 --> 00:05:59.648
At the end of my career,
that's how I look back on it

00:05:59.648 --> 00:06:02.646
and hope people will see me.

00:06:02.646 --> 00:06:06.315
Because I think over the years it's been,

00:06:06.315 --> 00:06:11.301
you know my life and my
career, people have obviously

00:06:11.301 --> 00:06:13.350
looked at certain other
things that have gone on

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.325
throughout my career and I think sometimes

00:06:16.325 --> 00:06:19.193
that's overshadowed what
I've done on the pitch

00:06:19.193 --> 00:06:22.018
or what I've achieved on the pitch.

00:06:22.018 --> 00:06:25.380
And that's as much as I say
that that doesn't hurt me,

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.883
of course it does, you
know at the end of the day,

00:06:27.883 --> 00:06:30.369
I'm a footballer that's
played for some of the biggest

00:06:30.369 --> 00:06:32.581
clubs in the world, played
with some of the best

00:06:32.581 --> 00:06:34.998
players in the world,
played under some of the

00:06:34.998 --> 00:06:39.026
biggest and best managers, and achieved

00:06:39.026 --> 00:06:41.557
almost everything in football.

00:06:41.557 --> 00:06:44.586
And I think of course
it hurts when people,

00:06:44.586 --> 00:06:46.939
not question it, but
think about other things,

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:50.580
and to come to the end of my career now,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.701
and look back and say
you know I've achieved

00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:56.822
everything with every
club that I've played for.

00:06:56.822 --> 00:07:00.242
I've played for my country 115 times,

00:07:00.242 --> 00:07:04.093
been runner up twice
world player of the year

00:07:04.093 --> 00:07:08.010
to amazing footballers,
I'm very proud of that.

00:07:11.236 --> 00:07:12.993
- I love how forward
this record, you had fans

00:07:12.993 --> 00:07:14.880
actually do little videos and talked about

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.735
what they were brave enough to do in life.

00:07:16.735 --> 00:07:18.510
So for you, what was
the moment you realized

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.150
you were brave enough to kind
of just do this fulltime,

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:23.218
and just go right after your passion?

00:07:23.218 --> 00:07:27.567
- Ooo, you know, I think it's
once I discovered YouTube.

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:30.316
I mean I had already been
going for it with full force,

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:33.866
you know, but I was
kind of, well wondering

00:07:33.866 --> 00:07:35.388
if had what it took to make it,

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:37.274
and I was really
discouraged at times because

00:07:37.274 --> 00:07:39.880
everywhere I went I
just kept being told no,

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.553
you're not good enough, and that can be

00:07:41.553 --> 00:07:42.738
really discouraging.

00:07:42.738 --> 00:07:44.257
It's like even though I was going for it,

00:07:44.257 --> 00:07:45.934
I was kind of like in the back of my mind,

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:48.083
just really scared, like
am I going to make it?

00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:50.804
I don't know, and then
when I finally discovered

00:07:50.804 --> 00:07:53.246
YouTube, and I put up my first video,

00:07:53.246 --> 00:07:55.859
I just felt so empowered and so excited

00:07:55.859 --> 00:07:58.742
because I was like whoa,
finally something is working.

00:07:58.742 --> 00:08:01.391
And that's when I was like I'm going to,

00:08:01.391 --> 00:08:02.733
you know I don't know how
this is going to work out,

00:08:02.733 --> 00:08:05.073
but I'm going to chase this
with everything I've got,

00:08:05.073 --> 00:08:07.694
and that's when I was like boom.

00:08:07.694 --> 00:08:10.175
- So success is not based on genetics.

00:08:10.175 --> 00:08:13.342
It's not based on how nice his car is.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.676
It's not based on how pretty my face is.

00:08:17.676 --> 00:08:19.912
How small my nose may need to look.

00:08:19.912 --> 00:08:24.443
You know, whether or not
I'm the right complexion.

00:08:24.443 --> 00:08:26.814
I have an eight inch scar
down the side of my face,

00:08:26.814 --> 00:08:31.707
but I have a camera in front
of me more often than not.

00:08:31.707 --> 00:08:34.612
Which just means that
you know if you work hard

00:08:34.612 --> 00:08:36.945
and your work is recognized,

00:08:38.811 --> 00:08:41.097
you know the sky's the limit.

00:08:41.097 --> 00:08:42.789
So for those people out
there that think they're ugly

00:08:42.789 --> 00:08:45.753
and everything, I'm going
to hold it down for you.

00:08:45.753 --> 00:08:49.343
But more importantly, you
can still be a success.

00:08:49.343 --> 00:08:51.258
For all those people who
think well I'm too short,

00:08:51.258 --> 00:08:54.574
well, I'm going to hold it down for you.

00:08:54.574 --> 00:08:56.976
And more importantly you
can still be a success.

00:08:56.976 --> 00:09:00.029
Find the things that you're excited about

00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:01.966
and that you can give your all

00:09:01.966 --> 00:09:05.622
and work really hard towards attaining.

00:09:05.622 --> 00:09:07.428
String those days with efficiency,

00:09:07.428 --> 00:09:11.178
and action together,
and success can happen.

